Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user has made two explicit "Please continue with the refactoring of the codebase." requests in this session, continuing an ongoing pure structural Extract Method refactoring effort on G005_termux (Android terminal emulator). The goal is improving structure and readability through behavior-preserving named method extractions, verified against the 143-test offline harness (`/tmp/tev/verify_full.sh`) before each commit.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - **Extract Method refactoring**: Verbatim body moves with no logic changes; all extractions behavior-preserving
   - **Test harness**: `/tmp/tev/verify_full.sh` — plain `javac` + `junit-4.13.2.jar` with Android stubs in `/tmp/tev/astub/`; produces 143 tests OK; must pass before each commit
   - **Early-return propagation**: When original code has `break` in a switch case that would skip nothing, `return` in extracted method is equivalent
   - **Static helpers**: Pure functions with no instance state become `private static`
   - **mArgIndex clamp pattern**: `if (mArgIndex >= mArgs.length) mArgIndex = mArgs.length - 1;` — repeated 5 times, extracted to `clampArgIndex()`
   - **XOR bit-flip equivalence**: `(effect & ~bits) | (bits & ~effect)` == `effect ^ bits`
   - **Double-negative simplification**: `!(!a && b)` == `(a || !b)`
   - **shiftTail contract**: Always keeps `mText` in sync with returned array (`mText = text = newText` inside); callers can access `mText` directly after calls
   - **ReflowState holder**: Static inner class grouping 5 mutable locals
   - **clampArgIndex** guard: defensive before iterating `mArgs[0..mArgIndex]`
   - **NEVER** use `git checkout <file>` to revert mutations — use Edit tool instead
   - Branch: `claude-exp/20260629T214200Z-claude-sonnet-4-6-high-Agent`
   - Primary working directory: `/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G005_termux`

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`terminal-emulator/src/main/java/com/termux/terminal/TerminalEmulator.java`** (primary target)
     - Most refactoring work occurs here
     - **`doBackspace()`** — extracted from `processCodePoint` case 8; handles auto-wrap line-unwrap:
       ```java
       private void doBackspace() {
           if (mLeftMargin == mCursorCol) {
               int previousRow = mCursorRow - 1;
               if (previousRow >= 0 && mScreen.getLineWrap(previousRow)) {
                   mScreen.clearLineWrap(previousRow);
                   setCursorRowCol(previousRow, mRightMargin - 1);
               }
           } else {
               setCursorCol(mCursorCol - 1);
           }
       }
       ```
     - **`doEscBackIndex()`** — extracted from `doEsc` case '6' (DECBI):
       ```java
       private void doEscBackIndex() {
           if (mCursorCol > mLeftMargin) {
               mCursorCol--;
           } else {
               int rows = mBottomMargin - mTopMargin;
               mScreen.blockCopy(mLeftMargin, mTopMargin, mRightMargin - mLeftMargin - 1, rows, mLeftMargin + 1, mTopMargin);
               mScreen.blockSet(mLeftMargin, mTopMargin, 1, rows, ' ', TextStyle.encode(mForeColor, mBackColor, 0));
           }
       }
       ```
